# Do not drop the local database

Never run drop, recreate, or volume-wipe database commands unless the user
explicitly asked for that in this conversation. Ask first. Wait for a clear yes.

`make db.migrate` and `make db.migrate.all` apply pending migrations only.
They do not drop databases. Do not pair them with `db.delete`.

## Forbidden without explicit approval

- `make db.delete`
- `make db.recreate.all.dangerous`
- `make dev.setup.no.cache` (`docker compose down -v`)
- `make dev.pr.clean.checkout`
- `dropdb`, `DROP DATABASE`, `migrate drop`
- Recreate sequences such as `db.delete` then `db.create` then `db.migrate`

A golang-migrate error such as `no migration found for version` is not
approval to drop `superplane_dev`. Stop and ask.

To refresh `db/structure.sql`, run `make db.migrate.all` only.
